# Test: a refused reload that auto-loaded a plugin whose startup handshake
#       failed reports doctor-config-reload-refused only, leaving no
#       doctor-plugin-stopped row or bus warning, keeping plugins health up,
#       and refusing `request plugin restart` for that unconfigured plugin.
#
# Question: when `request reload` adds an `mrt` section whose Stage 2
#   OnConfigure fails (RFC 6397 mixed WGS84/NaN coordinates: latitude set with
#   longitude omitted) so the reload is refused, do `show doctor` and `show
#   warnings` omit `doctor-plugin-stopped` for `mrt`, does `show health` keep
#   the `plugins` row `up`, and does `request plugin restart mrt` refuse it as
#   not a configured plugin?
# Why not a unit test: only a live daemon proves the full reload -> auto-load ->
#   Stage 2 failure -> rollback -> report bus -> doctor/warnings/health -> CLI
#   restart refusal path end to end.
#
# Spec: spec-plugin-restart-bounded-and-configuration-true AC-10
# VALIDATES: runPluginPhaseWithin skips pm.RecordStopped and unconfigures a
#   failed candidate reload auto-load so neither pm.configs nor pm.stopped nor
#   the doctor-plugin-stopped bus warning leaks into the running daemon.
# PREVENTS: a refused reload leaving `plugins` health down and `show warnings`
#   prescribing `ze request plugin restart <name>` for a plugin the committed
#   configuration never named.

option=needs-build-tag:value=ze_bgp:state=present
option=timeout:value=60s
option=env:var=ze.ssh.username:value=admin
option=env:var=ze.ssh.password:value=testpass
option=env:var=ze.ssh.port:value=$PORT

tmpfs=running.conf:terminator=EOF_BASE
system {
	authentication {
		# bcrypt cost-4 hash of "testpass".
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
		}
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT;
		}
	}
}
EOF_BASE

# Valid YANG, no InProcessConfigVerifier on mrt; mrt Stage 2 OnConfigure rejects
# mixed WGS84 latitude with omitted (NaN) longitude (RFC 6397 Section 4.1).
tmpfs=bad-mrt.conf:terminator=EOF_BAD_MRT
system {
	authentication {
		# bcrypt cost-4 hash of "testpass".
		user admin {
			password "$2a$04$UlwuiuH82Unfsq.XEMPGJeDkXwbm3KW.nvVaVXOd/JeFK8VjMjrQO"
		}
	}
}
environment {
	ssh {
		enabled true
		server main {
			ip 127.0.0.1;
			port $PORT;
		}
	}
}
mrt {
	routes {
		file "dump.mrt";
		interval 60;
		geo {
			enabled true;
			collector {
				latitude "10.0";
			}
		}
	}
}
EOF_BAD_MRT

tmpfs=swap-config.sh:mode=755:terminator=EOF_SWAP
#!/bin/sh
set -eu
cp "$1" running.conf
EOF_SWAP

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze start running.conf:name=daemon:ready=Ze running.
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=le test fixture daemon/await-answer plugins "show health | json":exit=0

# Swap in bad-mrt.conf and reload: mrt auto-loads and fails Stage 2 OnConfigure,
# so the reload is refused.
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=sh swap-config.sh bad-mrt.conf:exit=0
cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze cli -c "request reload":exit=1

# AC-10: doctor reports doctor-config-reload-refused and NO doctor-plugin-stopped.
cmd=foreground:seq=5:exec=ze cli -c "show doctor | json":exit=0
expect=stdout:contains="code": "doctor-config-reload-refused"
reject=stdout:contains=doctor-plugin-stopped
reject=stdout:contains=configured plugin mrt is not running

# AC-10: warnings carry no leaked doctor-plugin-stopped warning for mrt.
cmd=foreground:seq=6:exec=ze cli -c "show warnings | json":exit=0
reject=stdout:contains=doctor-plugin-stopped
reject=stdout:contains=configured plugin mrt is not running

# AC-10: plugins health stays up.
cmd=foreground:seq=7:exec=ze cli -c "show health | json":exit=0
expect=stdout:pattern="name":\s*"plugins",\s*"status":\s*"healthy"
reject=stdout:contains=configured plugin mrt is not running

# AC-10: mrt is not a configured plugin, so restart refuses it.
cmd=foreground:seq=8:exec=ze cli -c "request plugin restart mrt":exit=1
expect=stderr:contains=plugin mrt is not a configured plugin
expect=stderr:contains=only a plugin the configuration or its auto-load started can be restarted
expect=stderr:contains=ze show doctor, which names every configured plugin

cmd=stop:seq=9:name=daemon:signal=term
